loor, string course, arched windows of the piano nobile, cornice and balustrade, the entrance's projecting centre on St Martin's Place, the corner pavilions under slate; the top-lit galleries' glass lanterns, the glass rooftop restaurant of Dixon Jones's Ondaatje Wing (2000), Jamie Fobert's new doors on the north front (2023); the Cavell memorial on its island. Guessed: which of the outline's cells are the gallery and which the National Gallery's north range, heights (about 20 m), window rhythm, the lanterns' places, the context blocks' heights."}
